      <!-- HOWTO : BEGIN -->
      <div id="maboss_howto" class="hidden">
	<h3>How to build a mathematical model using MaBoSS</h3>
	<ol>
<!--	  <li>Install MaBoSS on your desktop (we advise to create a directory where the models and the program will be stored)</li> -->
	  <li class="vspace">Install MaBoSS on your desktop as described in the <a href="#" class="clean-link" onclick="show('installation');return false;">installation page</a></li>
	  <li class="vspace">Write the model using MaBoSS grammar in <span class="tt">file.bnd</span> (for instance):
	    <ul>
	      <li>write the logic for each node</li>
	      <li>assign parameter values to each transition rate</li>
	    </ul>
	  </li>
	  <li class="vspace">Write the configuration file <span class="tt">file.cfg</span> (for instance) to define the estimation, network, output and run parameters</li>
	  <li class="vspace">Run MaBoSS:
	    <ul>
	      <!--	      <li>open a terminal</li> -->
	      <!-- 	      <li>go to the MaBoSS directory created in 1.</li> -->
	      <li style="margin-top: 5px;" class="vspace">Type:
		<br>
		<span class="tt">MaBoSS -c file.cfg -o file_out file.bnd</span>
		<br>(we assume that MaBoSS is accessible through you PATH)</li>
	      <li class="vspace">MaBoSS creates two output files:
		<ul>
		  <li><span class="tt">file_out_proptraj.csv</span></li>
		  <li><span class="tt">file_out_statdist.csv</span></li>
		</ul>
	      </li>
	    </ul>
	  </li>
	  <li>Import output files in Excel or R</li>
	</ol>
	You will find more information in the MaBoSS reference card in the <a href="#" class="clean-link" onclick="show('documentation');return false;">documentation page</a>
      </div>
      <!-- HOWTO : END -->

